      "content": "but it's not even about being \"overwhelmed\" really. it's more like... a quiet realization. like a sunset. you don't fight the sun when it goes down, you just accept that the day is over. why is it so much harder for people to accept that some things are just meant to end? that maybe there's a certain dignity in just letting go when the time has passed?",
